                                                "text": "septic tank"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feb608b1-bb1b-47a6-a72d-eb39de606706",
                                                "sense_id": "001095cf-4e7f-3b22-92bf-8012fc69cde9",
                                                "text": "a septic system"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "septic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5df89f71-e242-332e-8a1d-1c1834dedcde",
                                        "entry_id": "e4bdd7ac-4eb2-3527-9d5d-77e0cb854254",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A substance that causes sepsis or putrefaction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5897a4ee-b79f-4a3c-a63a-ca3411aeea2e",
                                                "sense_id": "5df89f71-e242-332e-8a1d-1c1834dedcde",
                                                "text": "1750, John Pringle, Further Experiments on Substances Resisting Putrefaction, in 1809, Charles Hutton, George Shaw, Richard Pearson (editors), The Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society of London, Volume X: 1750—1755, page 86,\nBut, in the prosecution of this subject, he had met with very few real septics; and found many substances, commonly accounted such, of a quite opposite nature."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89b00d51-5ec9-304a-8419-ed1fd7c6ad67",
                                        "entry_id": "e4bdd7ac-4eb2-3527-9d5d-77e0cb854254",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who has sepsis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad32c482-f3b9-4dbb-8b5a-0e458c684f8d",
                                                "sense_id": "89b00d51-5ec9-304a-8419-ed1fd7c6ad67",
                                                "text": "Acid-base balance data revealed moderately abnormal metabolic balance for both septics and nonseptics (in either direction) with normal respiratory balance or mild alkalosis."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fdd3164d-8892-3b7c-8549-f1e2c2bb95be",
                                        "entry_id": "e4bdd7ac-4eb2-3527-9d5d-77e0cb854254",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A septic tank; a system for the disposal of sewage into a septic tank, a septic system."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b6ef7b5-cacc-4368-9618-87458863b4ed",
                                                "sense_id": "fdd3164d-8892-3b7c-8549-f1e2c2bb95be",
                                                "text": "The question is whether there are any spatial differences in how septics impact water quality, and whether these spatial variations should be considered when regulating septic improvement or removal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "septic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0b11e8e-20cc-3fa1-965d-16e8c048b318",
                                        "entry_id": "7a94776e-3268-3e86-aa57-de4067a1b58a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mathematical object (function, curve, surface, etc.) of degree seven."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7196e7d-e97b-4860-8ad3-4f7a2648434e",
                                                "sense_id": "f0b11e8e-20cc-3fa1-965d-16e8c048b318",
                                                "text": "Enriques states that it is possible to construct a family of septics with a singular curve of degree 7 and genus 4 having a triple point that degenerates to the above configuration[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e90e4222-ebda-45f6-baa7-0f92e56ed322",
                                                "sense_id": "f0b11e8e-20cc-3fa1-965d-16e8c048b318",
                                                "text": "Now consider the two septics C = U⁷ᵢ₌₁Cᵢ, D = U⁷ᵢ₌₁Dᵢ and note that for i = 1,2,3,4,5,6 the lines Cᵢ and Dᵢ are parallel, so that the intersection of two septics S' consists of 6⁶^([sic]) + 6 + 1 = 43 points and it is the singular set of a foliation of degree 6."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "septic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "690a2241-2a01-39a1-b0ad-477f8b3dac57",
                                        "entry_id": "983131de-09d0-3126-b4d3-8795a06bd015",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the seventh degree or order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "septic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "168f241c-c553-375b-ada9-3f5751ea6d7a",
                                        "entry_id": "13e308e5-5fd0-3463-a4bc-489bc2bbb4c0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An American, a Yank."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "New-Zealand",
                                            "UK",
                                            "ethnic",
                                            "slang",
                                            "slur"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3799eae7-3c5f-4929-aef0-70f07729624e",
                                                "sense_id": "168f241c-c553-375b-ada9-3f5751ea6d7a",
                                                "text": "Typical septic. Can't understand why the rest of the world thinks he's a fuck-knuckle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "840d0151-e3fc-4e4c-ab19-63eb9b5ae11b",
                                                "sense_id": "168f241c-c553-375b-ada9-3f5751ea6d7a",
                                                "text": "“Didn′t enjoy the septics,” he says jokingly about the Americans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0adbf7a-815e-4c75-9ef4-01c23c65576d",
                                                "sense_id": "168f241c-c553-375b-ada9-3f5751ea6d7a",
                                                "text": "“What′s the septics′ Achilles heel?” I said using the slang septic tank, meaning Yank."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
